t","code":"def select_next_node(current_node: int, depot: int, unvisited_nodes: np.ndarray,\n                     rest_capacity: float, demands: np.ndarray,\n                     distance_matrix: np.ndarray) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Select the next node to visit in a CVRP greedy construction.\n\n    Args:\n        current_node:    index of the current node (0 = depot)\n        depot:           index of the depot (always 0)\n        unvisited_nodes: array of feasible unvisited customer indices\n                         (already filtered to satisfy remaining capacity)\n        rest_capacity:   remaining vehicle capacity\n        demands:         demand of every node (index 0 = depot demand = 0)\n        distance_matrix: pairwise Euclidean distance matrix\n    Returns:\n        Index of the next node to visit, or 0 to return to the depot early.\n    \"\"\"\n    if unvisited_nodes.size == 0:\n        return depot\n\n    d_cur = distance_matrix[current_node][unvisited_nodes]\n    d_dep = distance_matrix[depot][unvisited_nodes]\n    dem = demands[unvisited_nodes]\n\n    # Savings of inserting a node between current position and depot:\n    # serving it now avoids a separate depot round-trip later.\n    savings = distance_matrix[current_node][depot] + d_dep - d_cur\n\n    # Normalise demand influence so heavier (harder-to-place) customers\n    # get a mild priority when their insertion cost is low.\n    dem_norm = dem / (rest_capacity + 1e-9)\n\n    # Composite score: we want high savings, low detour, prefer heavier\n    # demands slightly, and avoid long repositioning.\n    scores = -savings + 0.30 * d_cur - 0.15 * d_dep - 0.25 * dem_norm * d_cur\n\n    return int(unvisited_nodes[np.argmin(scores)])","code_sha256":"4227bf42a78fc959757bbe21a74e5197bfa5f28cc02fa784ef84ce09b0e5f68a","elapsed_seconds":0.391,"error_code":null,"error_detail":null,"evaluation_id":"76d2a75f4c004c3ea1ea57b7f2937029","generation_parents":null,"generation_request_ref":null,"instance_objectives":[10.040613